---
Add a "Random" feature for drum patterns and kits.

Inspired by the "mystery rig" feature in 0xFX and the "random"
preset in 0xSYNTH. The user wants a one-click way to discover
new groove starting points.

Scope (propose in two tiers — implement tier 1, gate tier 2 on
feedback):

Tier 1 — Random pattern only:
- Toolbar button + keyboard shortcut (e.g. Ctrl+R)
- Generates a musically plausible 16-step pattern across
  current sampler tracks (kick on 1/9, snare on 5/13, hats
  filled in with weighted velocity, percussion sparse)
- Uses current kit; does not change the kit
- Writes to current pattern slot, undoable

Tier 2 — Random kit:
- Optional checkbox / second button that also rolls the kit
  (cycles through sq_kits[] or — once TASK-224 lands —
  randomly picks from a wider auto-imported pool)

Heuristics > pure RNG: hard-code per-track step probabilities
and velocity distributions so output sounds intentional. See
how 0xFX mystery-rig biases parameter ranges for reference.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] "Random" button visible on toolbar (both ImGui + GTK)
- [ ] Generates a 16-step pattern that plays without sounding
      like white noise — kick/snare on the right beats
- [ ] Action is undoable (uses existing sq_undo machinery)
- [ ] Optional "Random Kit" toggle or secondary action
- [ ] Keyboard shortcut wired up in src/app/sq_app.c key handler
- [ ] Frontend parity (ImGui + GTK)

## Test Plan
- [ ] Click Random 10x, verify each pattern is distinct and
      musically usable
- [ ] Verify undo restores prior pattern
- [ ] Verify RNG seeded so successive runs differ
